-- ProfileTag — a manual classification tag on a profile, with optional
-- validity window and importance score. The importance score is a
-- refined-Number in [0..1] wrapped in Maybe (an absent score is
-- distinct from a zero score).
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity (label / description / icon) is
-- registered by defineSystemEntity on the TS side.
--
-- Phase 3c of the system-entities sweep — see
-- workstreams/ts-elimination/briefs/phase-3c-profile-relations.md.
-- `Importance` is extracted as a top-level refined-Number atom for
-- the same reason as country.fenel's Latitude / Longitude — `|`
-- predicate-refinement is a type-decl-level form only and doesn't
-- parse at field-position type-expr slot. `Maybe Importance` then
-- works as a standard juxtaposition: a single-ident arg is consumed
-- by `parseTypeAppArg`'s ident branch directly, no parens needed.
-- The brief's Watch-out §2 documents both alternatives; this picks
-- path (b) (named-atom extraction), matching the Phase 3b precedent.

@entity
@label "Importance"
@description "Refined Number in [0, 1] — relative weighting for tags"
Importance = Number | value ∈ [0..1]

@entity
@codeName "profile_tag"
@label "Profile Tag"
@description "A manual classification tag on a profile (with optional validity window)"
@icon "tag"
@fieldLabel "profileId" "Profile"
ProfileTag = ProfileTag profileId: EntityRef<"profile"> tag: String context: Maybe String importance: Maybe Importance validFrom: Maybe Date validTo: Maybe Date
